 therapy with gemcitabine and radiotherapy as a bladder preservation strategy: results of a phase i trial</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2004</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>2540</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15226322</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-co16-4-36"><label>7</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rodel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Grabenbauer</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuhn</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Combined-modality treatment and selective organ preservation in invasive bladder cancer: long-term results</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2002</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>3061</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12118019</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-co16-4-36"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sangar</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name><name><surname>McBain</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyons</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Phase i study of conformal radiotherapy with concurrent gemcitabine in locally advanced bladder cancer</article-title><source>Int J Radiat Oncol Biol Phys</source><year>2005</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>420</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15667962</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-co16-4-36"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shipley</surname><given-names>WU</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaufman</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Zehr</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Selective bladder preservation by combined modality protocol treatment: long-term outcomes of 190 patients with invasive bladder cancer</article-title><source>Urology</source><year>2002</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>62</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12100923</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-co16-4-36"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cruciani</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dazzi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Montanari</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Conservative treatment for T2&#x02013;T4 bladder cancer with primary chemotherapy and radiotherapy: a pilot study</article-title><source>Tumori</source><year>1993</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8497923</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-co16-4-36"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fellin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Graffer</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolner</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ambrosini</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Caffo</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Luciani</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Combined chemotherapy and radiation with selective organ preservation for muscle-invasive bladder carcinoma. A single-institution phase ii study</article-title><source>Br J Urol</source><year>1997</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>44</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9240179</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-co16-4-36"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmitt</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Armand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mille</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Favrel&#x02013;Tchakamian</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilloz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Concurrent chemotherapy and hyperfractionated radiotherapy for non-operable carcinoma of the bladder [French]</article-title><source>Cancer Radiother</source><year>1998</year><volume>2</volume><issue>suppl 1</issue><fpage>82s</fpage><lpage>4s</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9749085</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-co16-4-36"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arias</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Dominguez</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Chemoradiotherapy for muscle invading bladder carcinoma. Final report of a single institutional organ-sparing program</article-title><source>Int J Radiat Oncol Biol Phys</source><year>2000</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>373</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10802362</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-co16-4-36"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cobo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Delgado</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gil</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Conservative treatment with transurethral resection, neoadjuvant chemotherapy followed by radiochemotherapy in stage T2&#x02013;3 transitional bladder cancer</article-title><source>Clin Transl Oncol</source><year>2006</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>903</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17169764</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref